# Rust
target/
Cargo.lock

# Python
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
__pycache__/
.venv/

# Internal design material lives in the private pretium-design repo,
# never in this one. docs/ holds the public documentation.

# Spike artifacts
dist-spike/
.venv-spike/

# Golden vectors ARE committed: they are the parity contract, and a research
# library whose tests cannot run on a fresh clone is not checkable by anyone.
# 135 MB raw. See rust/sync-goldens.py for how they are produced, and
# CONTINUE.md for the compression decision still to make (85% available).

# Build artefacts from `maturin develop`, which writes the compiled extension
# and its debug symbols straight into the source tree. They are 2 MB, they
# change on every rebuild, and a wheel is the only thing anyone should be
# installing.
# The path is `python/tradefloor/` and was `python/pretium/` until the rename.
# These three lines kept the old path, so `maturin develop` began writing an
# UNIGNORED 1.1 MB extension and a 1.0 MB debug database into the tree; both
# were committed, the stale extension then shadowed the real one for anyone
# importing from the source directory, and `pretium.pdb` shipped inside every
# published wheel. Match the directory that exists, and both, so a rename
# cannot quietly re-open this.
python/tradefloor/*.pyd
python/tradefloor/*.so
python/tradefloor/*.pdb
python/pretium/*.pyd
python/pretium/*.so
python/pretium/*.pdb

# Test and tool caches. `.impeccable` is a product-spec tool's working
# directory -- a JSON cache and 2.9 MB of docs-site screenshots. Neither is
# source, and neither belongs in the artifact a user clones to get an engine.
.pytest_cache/
.impeccable/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Editor and OS artefacts. .DS_Store was tracked at the repository root until
# 0.1.2, which a public repository should not carry: it is a Finder cache,
# it changes whenever a directory is viewed, and it means nothing to anyone
# cloning. It never reached the distribution, so this is tidiness rather
# than a shipped defect.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Experiment artifacts written by a study under examples/. Output, not input:
# regenerable by running the study again, and describing one run rather than
# the repository. The recorded inputs a study REPLAYS are a different thing
# and are committed, under tests/fixtures/. See CONTRIBUTING.md.
examples/*/artifacts/
